accTitle: Selected supply-chain domain relationships
accDescr: A customer order contains order lines for products. Inventory lots hold products at locations and reservations connect lots to order lines. Suppliers qualify for products and receive purchase orders. Carriers support routes and carry shipments whose lines serve order lines. Disruptions are related to recovery objectives and proposed recovery candidates.
flowchart LR
    Product[Product] -->|required by| OrderLine[Order line]
    Product -->|qualified for| Capability[Supplier product capability]
    Product -->|held in| Lot[Inventory lot]
    Location[Inventory location] -->|stores| Lot
    Supplier[Supplier] -->|owns| Capability
    Supplier -->|receives| PO[Purchase order]
    PO -->|orders| Product
    Order[Customer order] -->|contains| OrderLine
    Lot -->|allocated through| Reservation[Reservation]
    Reservation -->|fulfils| OrderLine
    Carrier[Carrier] -->|supports| Route[Route]
    Carrier -->|carries| Shipment[Shipment]
    Shipment -->|uses| Route
    Shipment -->|serves| OrderLine
    Disruption[Disruption] -->|motivates| Objective[Recovery objective]
    Objective -->|has proposals| Candidate[Recovery candidate]
    Candidate -->|contains typed| Action[Recovery action]
